  "fullText": "**1. The psychology of “external brain” – why off‑loading tasks to tools (apps, lists, voice notes) reduces mental load and improves focus, backed by research on cognitive load theory.  \n\n**2. Hybrid systems vs. pure digital:** compare the strengths of paper / bullet‑journal methods (tactile feedback, habit formation) with digital platforms (automation, cross‑device sync, reminders), and show how many high‑performers blend both.  \n\n**3. Timing tricks that actually work:** explore evidence‑based reminder strategies (e.g., “time‑boxing”, “the two‑minute rule”, spaced‑repetition for recurring tasks) and how smart‑assistant integrations can enforce them without feeling intrusive.",
